PANIM: TDLib makes no connection that does not use the proxy.

This patch is for TDLib 1.8.68 (commit c15d3f5a5de6e3ba5839822c451152e5e18bb700). `flake.nix` applies it.
`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` §4b and `spikes/tdlib/README.md` give the reasons and the proof.

Without the patch, TDLib goes past the proxy of the persona in these cases:

- The state is "Connecting" for 5 seconds. Then the "config recovery" asks Google DNS, Mozilla DNS, Azure and
  Firebase for new addresses of Telegram, with direct HTTPS requests. It can then connect directly to a Telegram
  address to get the full configuration.
- The proxy has a host name. Then TDLib asks Google DNS and the resolver of the system for its address.

The patch has four changes:

1. `td/telegram/ConfigManager.cpp`, `ConfigRecoverer::loop`: the loop returns immediately. Thus, TDLib starts no
   config recovery: no simple configuration request and no full configuration request.
2. `td/telegram/net/ConnectionCreator.cpp`, `request_raw_connection_by_ip`: the function gives an error. It makes a
   connection to an address without the proxy. Only the config recovery calls it. This change is a second
   protection.
3. `tdnet/td/net/Wget.cpp`, `Wget::try_init`: the function gives an error. `Wget` is the HTTP client of TDLib, and
   it has no proxy support. The config recovery and the Google DNS resolver use it. Thus, TDLib makes no HTTP
   request.
4. `tdnet/td/net/GetHostByNameActor.cpp`, `NativeDnsResolver`: the resolver accepts only an IPv4 or IPv6 address.
   It does not call `getaddrinfo` for a host name. Thus, a proxy with a host name gives an error and no lookup.

The patch does not change these parts, because they run only when the app sends the request:

- `pingProxy` with no proxy connects directly to Telegram.
- `testProxy` connects to the proxy that the request gives, and it can look up its host name.

PANIM sends none of these requests.

Known limit: on a network that blocks the built-in addresses of Telegram, TDLib cannot find new addresses.

diff -ru a/td/telegram/ConfigManager.cpp b/td/telegram/ConfigManager.cpp
--- a/td/telegram/ConfigManager.cpp
+++ b/td/telegram/ConfigManager.cpp
@@ -712,6 +712,10 @@
     if (close_flag_) {
       return;
     }
+    // PANIM: no config recovery. It does not use the proxy.
+    if (true) {
+      return;
+    }
     if (Session::is_high_loaded()) {
       VLOG(config_recoverer) << "Skip config recoverer under high load";
       set_timeout_in(Random::fast(200, 300));
diff -ru a/td/telegram/net/ConnectionCreator.cpp b/td/telegram/net/ConnectionCreator.cpp
--- a/td/telegram/net/ConnectionCreator.cpp
+++ b/td/telegram/net/ConnectionCreator.cpp
@@ -601,6 +601,10 @@
 
 void ConnectionCreator::request_raw_connection_by_ip(IPAddress ip_address, mtproto::TransportType transport_type,
                                                      Promise<unique_ptr<mtproto::RawConnection>> promise) {
+  // PANIM: this connection does not use the proxy.
+  if (true) {
+    return promise.set_error(400, "Direct connections are off");
+  }
   TRY_RESULT_PROMISE(promise, socket_fd, SocketFd::open(ip_address));
 
   auto connection_promise = PromiseCreator::lambda([actor_id = actor_id(this), promise = std::move(promise),
